  data: {
    LLM: '1. Draw one card from the stock or the top of the discard pile. 2. Optionally meld sets (3–4 of a rank) or runs (3+ consecutive same suit). 3. Optionally lay off cards on existing melds. 4. Discard one card face up to end your turn. 5. First to empty their hand ends the hand; hands are then evaluated or scored using poker hand rankings.',
    Player: '1. Draw one card from the stock or the top of the discard pile. 2. Optionally meld sets (3–4 of a rank) or runs (3+ consecutive same suit). 3. Optionally lay off cards on existing melds. 4. Discard one card face up to end your turn. 5. First to empty their hand ends the hand; hands are then evaluated or scored using poker hand rankings.',
    objective: 'Dispose of all cards by melding and discarding; when a hand ends, outcome or scoring is determined using standard poker hand rankings (e.g. best five-card poker hand from melds or deadwood).',
    gameplay: '1. Draw one card from the stock or the top of the discard pile. 2. Optionally meld sets (3–4 of a rank) or runs (3+ consecutive same suit). 3. Optionally lay off cards on existing melds. 4. Discard one card face up to end your turn. 5. First to empty their hand ends the hand; hands are then evaluated or scored using poker hand rankings.',
    keyRules: [
      'Melds are sets (3–4 of a rank) or runs (3+ in suit).',
      'Lay off is allowed on any meld on the table.',
      'One draw and one discard per turn.',
      'Poker hand rankings (high card through straight flush) determine scoring or winner when applied to the hand result.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
