    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 7 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Dispose of all cards by melding and discarding; when a hand ends, outcome or scoring is determined using standard poker hand rankings (e.g. best five-card poker hand from melds or deadwood).',
      'Turn-flow example: 1. Draw one card from the stock or the top of the discard pile. 2. Optionally meld sets (3–4 of a rank) or runs (3+ consecutive same suit). 3. Optionally lay off cards on existing melds. 4. Discard one card face up to end your turn. 5. First to empty their hand ends the hand; hands are then evaluated or scored using poker hand rankings.',
      'Scoring example: When a player goes out, hands are evaluated using standard poker hand rankings (high card, pair, two pair, flush, full house, etc.); winner or scores determined by agreed variant (e.g. best poker hand from melds or deadwood). First to reach agreed target score or win the most hands; each hand outcome determined by poker hand ranking..',
